# About / Summary web–mobile alignment

Channel **About** and item **Summary** must carry the **same information** on web and mobile.
Vocabulary for description / About / Summary lives in **domain-terms**.

## Required content

| Surface | Always includes | Never |
| ------- | --------------- | ----- |
| Channel About (podcast, album, artist) | `channel_description` | People, and falling back to item people |
| Item Summary (episode, track, livestream, full player) | `item_description` | People, and falling back to `channel_persons` |

People are their own chip (`info.people.people`), and on desktop channel pages their own
side-column block. Show that chip whenever the matching person array is non-empty, even if
description prose is empty. Channel screens use `channel_persons`. Item screens use
`item_persons`. Do not hide people behind an empty-description gate, and do not render people
inside About or Summary.

## Previews and full notes

List rows on web and mobile read the stored `preview` (`getDescriptionPreviewText`), and the full
notes load on detail. Mobile Summary reads them through `useItemDescription`, which falls back to
the on-device notes cache and then the description endpoint, so a Summary never depends on a list
payload carrying the whole description.

## Length (mobile)

Feed authors can paste unbounded HTML into channel description and item summary. On mobile,
**About** and **Summary** prose (podcast / album / artist About; episode / track / livestream /
full-player Summary) must **truncate by default** with **Show more** / **Show less**
(`info.show_more` / `info.show_less`). Do not render the full string until the user expands it.
Reset expanded state when the entity changes.

Episode, track, livestream, and channel About use a **720**-character collapsed preview.

The full-player Summary sits in a height-locked sheet. The card keeps `spacing.base` above and
below the scrolling text, and that inset stays while the text moves. Its collapsed preview is
plain text long enough to fill the area inside that inset and continue a little past it, so the
card reads as full and **Show more** sits just below the fold. A short scroll reaches the
control. The cut still exists so a very long description is not mounted until the listener
expands it. The sheet scrolling does not replace that truncate.

## Placement divergence (intentional)

Web has more screen width and keeps RSS, website, and funding as **always-visible header
icons**. Mobile tucks RSS and website into **About** so the identity block does not grow an
icon row. Funding is **not** an About body link on mobile: it is its own chip after the other
content chips, and only when that surface has funding rows (channel screens use
`channel_fundings`; item screens use `item_fundings` with no channel fallback). On channel
detail (podcast, album, artist), Settings is the gear at the top right of the channel header,
signed in or not. People, when that channel has people, is the last section chip, after Funding.
With no people, Funding is the last content chip. Only the optional sort / category trailing chip
may follow. Episode, track, and full-player screens have no channel-header gear, so People follows
Funding there.

| Field | Web | Mobile |
| ----- | --- | ------ |
| Description | About / Summary body | About / Summary body |
| People | People tab. On podcast, album, and artist it is hidden on desktop the same way About is, and the side column shows people as their own block. Episode, track, and livestream keep the tab on every viewport. | People chip after Funding |
| RSS, website | Header icons | About body links |
| Funding | Header icon | Funding chip (before People when the channel has people) |
| Share, subscribe, notifications, boost | Header / actions | Header / actions — not About body |
| Shortened notes | A link after the prose: the item link on Summary, the website on About | Summary: the same link after the expanded prose. About: the sentence only, because the website link is already in About |

Do **not** “fix” mobile by copying web header icons for RSS or website, and do **not** drop
those links from mobile About. Do **not** put funding links back into About.

## Adding fields

Adding a new About or Summary field on one surface requires the matching field on the other,
unless the plan records an intentional divergence (same pattern as the RSS/website/funding
placement above).

## Out of scope for this rule

Location, social interact, license, trailer, and other podcast-namespace tags are stored but
not part of the About/Summary body contract until both surfaces adopt them together.
